# End-to-end proof against real networks
# Generated 2026-08-22T16:36:57Z by packages/policy-synth/scripts/e2e-network.ts
#
# Each run deploys a FRESH smart account with TWO keys: an admin on rule 0
# (no policy, full authority) and an agent on rule 1 ONLY (policed,
# transfer-only). It then shows the permitted call succeeding, the forbidden
# call denied by the interpreter (#100 ArgMismatch), and the forbidden call
# still blocked when the agent tries to route it through the unpoliced rule.
#
# The last step is load-bearing: OZ takes the authority of the rule the
# CALLER NAMES, so a key on both a policed and an unpoliced rule is not
# constrained at all. The agent is on the policed rule only.

